course: dictionary
lesson: 9848
title: Sword: a word with a long history
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A sword is a weapon with a long, sharp metal blade and a handle called a hilt. People used swords long ago to fight. The context shows this: «The Rat packs a belt, a sword, a cutlass, a pair of pistols and a flask», so a sword sits with other weapons and gear for an expedition.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Cross swords» means to argue, and a «double-edged sword» is something that is both good and bad at once. Read the words around the phrase to find its meaning, because nobody is really holding a blade when people cross swords.
explain: Always swap your meaning into the sentence. In «swords are beaten into ploughshares», if a sword is a weapon, then the idea makes sense: weapons are turned into farm tools. Try your meaning first, and only use a dictionary when the context does not settle it.
fact: A sword is a weapon with a long, sharp metal blade and a handle called a hilt.
fact: «Sword» is a noun: one sword, two swords.
fact: Knights, Romans, Vikings and samurai fought with swords long ago.
fact: «Cross swords» means to argue, and a «double-edged sword» is something that is both good and bad at once.
fact: Children often play with toy or foam swords, and «sword fighting» is the sport of fencing.
exercise: «The Rat packs a belt, a sword, a cutlass, a pair of pistols and a flask.» Which item is a weapon with a long, sharp blade? | a belt | a flask | *a sword
exercise: Ella says, «They crossed swords about who should pay.» What does crossed swords mean here? | They played a game | They were best friends | They drew real blades | *They argued
exercise: What does «double-edged sword» mean? | A very sharp kitchen knife | A fight between two people | *Something that is both good and bad at once | A sword with two handles
test: Copy the word from «swords are beaten into ploughshares» that means farm tools. | dreamed | *ploughshares | world | prophet
test: What is the handle of a sword called? | blade | *hilt | fencing | ploughshare
exam: Which best describes a sword? | A kind of bird that swims | *A weapon with a long, sharp metal blade and a handle | A tool for digging gardens | A soft cloth for cleaning
